INT. VANTAGE BRANDS - CONFERENCE ROOM 4B - DAY

A glass box with a view of a parking structure. Whiteboard marker dries in its tray. A tray of untouched fruit.

CLAUDETTE ABERNETHY-FOX, forties, VP of Culture, stands at the screen with a clicker. ROMAN DZIEDZIC, thirties, a senior analyst, sits with a printout. PHILOMENA "PHIL" ARCHULETA, fifties, the new CFO, sits at the head of the table in a coat she hasn't removed.

CLAUDETTE
Welcome to the all-hands pre-read. I'll start with the good news.

ROMAN
There's good news?

CLAUDETTE
I'm going to need you to trust me.

PHIL
I'm listening.

Claudette clicks. A slide appears: a giant smiling sun and the words WE ARE A FAMILY.

CLAUDETTE
We are a family.

ROMAN
We laid off forty people on Monday.

CLAUDETTE
Families have difficult conversations.

ROMAN
Families don't usually fire each other by email.

PHIL
Roman.

ROMAN
I'm only saying.

CLAUDETTE
We prefer the term "restructured."

ROMAN
They prefer the term "fired."

Claudette clicks. A second slide: a graph of declining revenue, titled "GROWTH OPPORTUNITIES."

PHIL
Can I ask a basic question?

CLAUDETTE
Please.

PHIL
Where does the revenue go?

CLAUDETTE
It goes into the future.

ROMAN
It goes into the Culture budget.

CLAUDETTE
Which is the future.

PHIL
Claudette, your Culture budget is larger than engineering.

CLAUDETTE
Culture is engineering.

PHIL
Culture is a line item.

CLAUDETTE ^
Phil, with respect--

PHIL
(over her)
With respect, I read the line items.

They stare at each other. Roman reaches for a strawberry, eats it, and eats another.

CLAUDETTE
I'll circulate a deck.

PHIL
Please do.

ROMAN
Will there be a pre-read for the pre-read?

CLAUDETTE
Yes, Roman. There will.

She clicks to a third slide: a photograph of a golden retriever puppy with the words LET'S GO TOGETHER. Nobody speaks. The fruit tray, mostly full, sits in the center like a witness.

PHIL
I'm going to need to see a puppy budget.
